{
  "dom_id": "step-q213000",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA=\\{\\{5\\},\\{3,5\\},\\{1,3,5\\}\\}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following ordered pairs is an element of the relation \"is **not** a subset of\" on $A?$ \n\nI. $(\\{5\\},\\{5\\})$\n\nII. $(\\{5\\},\\{3,5\\})$\n\nIII. $(\\{3,5\\},\\{5\\})$",
  "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {A}^{2}$ such that $x⊈y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our ordered pairs in turn.\n\n- The ordered pair $(\\{5\\},\\{5\\})$ is **not** an element of $R$ since $\\{5\\}⊆\\{5\\}.\\,\\times $\n\n- The ordered pair $(\\{5\\},\\{3,5\\})$ is **not** an element of $R$ since $\\{5\\}⊆\\{3,5\\}.\\,\\times $\n\n- The ordered pair $(\\{3,5\\},\\{5\\})$ is an element of $R$ since $\\{3,5\\}⊈\\{5\\}.\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
